// The iron spit, and the one thing it is for.
//
// The spit is smithed from an iron bar at 17 Smithing and then, before this, did nothing at all -
// the playtest report's "iron spit - nothing interesting happens". Its use is cooking: thread raw
// meat onto it and the skewered meat goes on a fire. Raw rabbit was the other half of the same
// dead end - it drops from every rabbit and the charter shop stocks twenty of them, and there was
// no way to cook one. Both the skewered rabbit and the roast rabbit have been sitting in the 377
// cache since 20 February 2006, models and all, waiting for these few lines.
//
// The spit is a tool, not an ingredient: it stays in the inventory, so one spit does a whole
// trip's worth of rabbits. https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Iron_spit
//
// The cooking half is an ordinary cooking_generic row (skill_cooking/configs/cooking_source), so
// the skewered rabbit goes through the same burn curve, batch loop and Cook-X window as any other
// food, and only over a fire - a range has nowhere to rest a spit. Eating the roast needs nothing
// new: the opheld audit already gave it a handler and a 7-hitpoint heal, and the Hitpoints guide
// has listed it all along. The food simply could not be reached.
[opheldu,spit_iron]
switch_obj(last_useitem) {
    case raw_rabbit :
        inv_del(inv, raw_rabbit, 1);
        inv_add(inv, spit_skewered_rabbit_meat, 1);
        mes("You skewer the rabbit on the iron spit.");
    case default : ~displaymessage(^dm_default);
}
